[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I am researching formatter for lean 4. There are a couple of github repos. But it seems to me none of them implemented the recommended style guide (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/doc/std/style.md\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/doc/std/style.md</a>).</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/codygunton/lean-fmt\">https://github.com/codygunton/lean-fmt</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/toku-sa-n/leanfmt\">https://github.com/toku-sa-n/leanfmt</a>). Are there 'official' supported formatter that implements the recommended style guide?</p>",
        "id": 603898840,
        "sender_full_name": "Zhi Han",
        "timestamp": 1781639477
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not yet, but it’s coming.</p>",
        "id": 603900276,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1781639847
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There's also an <a href=\"https://github.com/wvhulle/pretty-lean\">unofficial Lean fork by wvhulle</a> with a formatter which is what I've been using for the past few months.</p>",
        "id": 604334694,
        "sender_full_name": "Anthony Wang",
        "timestamp": 1781742210
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I couldn't wait and made one myself (<a href=\"https://github.com/duckki/LeanFmt\">https://github.com/duckki/LeanFmt</a>), partly because my preference is slightly different from Lean community guidance.</p>\n<p>I want operators to lead wrapped-around lines like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parenthesizedConjunctionChain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Schema</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">namesAreUnique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">allTypes</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TypeDefinition</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">objectType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">queryType</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeDefinition</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">typeDefinition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">types</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeDefinitionWellFormed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeDefinition</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">objectTypeName</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">objectTypeName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getPossibleTypes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeName</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">schema</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">objectType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">objectTypeName</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It works well on my project (<a href=\"https://github.com/duckki/GraphQL.lean\">https://github.com/duckki/GraphQL.lean</a>).<br>\nI'm currently going though mathlib for robustness. I think I can finish it in about a week.</p>",
        "id": 611917973,
        "sender_full_name": "Duckki",
        "timestamp": 1784647223
    }
]